## Shapes that select nodes Semantica actually stores.
##
## ddl-comprehensive shapes.ttl uses sh:targetClass on domain classes
## (AIEngine, ALPARC, ...). Those shapes validate instances. Semantica's
## OWL load keeps classes and properties, not named individuals, so the
## generated file selects no focus nodes.
##
## Aegir's SHACL emit (realize_sdg.py via `kvasir shapes`) should also write
## a profile whose targets are the SKOS concepts and TBox terms that get
## loaded, or emit one exemplar individual per targetClass. This file is
## that profile for the feature probe.
##
## Validate it against the concept scheme
## (https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme), not the OWL ontology IRI.
## A concept that carries scheme_uri is owned by the scheme, so it is
## absent from the ontology data graph and both minCounts fail there
## even when the notation is stored. Against the scheme, the notation
## shape conforms and the example shape reports the missing skos:example.

@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/shape/probe-notation>
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetNode <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SemanticaFeatureProbe> ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path skos:notation ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
    ] .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/shape/probe-example>
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetNode <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SemanticaFeatureProbe> ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path skos:example ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:name "example" ;
        sh:message "Aegir does not emit skos:example, and Semantica's concept detail has no example field." ;
    ] .
